 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
--   **Bias Correction:** Importance sampling introduces bias by preferentially selecting directions. The final radiance contribution must be divided by the calculated PDF to ensure an unbiased estimator [S1, unofficial].
--   **Precision:** Walking the CDF arrays requires careful handling of floating-point comparisons. If the random number equals the CDF value exactly, the loop condition `<=` ensures the next index is selected, which is consistent with standard inverse transform sampling definitions [G].
